-- title:
--   §2, pp. 2–4 — the continuous-time skip-free Markov chain generated by a Q-matrix: transition function, resolvent, hitting and exit probabilities, killed and dual chains
-- statement:
--   Let $E=[\mathfrak l,\mathfrak h]\cap\mathbb Z$ with $\mathfrak l<\mathfrak h$ in $\mathbb Z\cup\{\pm\infty\}$, and let $Q=(Q(x,y))_{x,y\in E}$ be a **Q-matrix** on $E$: $0\le Q(x,y)<\infty$ for $x\ne y$ and $\sum_{y\ne x}Q(x,y)\le Q(x):=-Q(x,x)<\infty$. The matrix need not be conservative: the **killing rate** is $Q(x,\partial)=Q(x)-\sum_{y\ne x}Q(x,y)\ge 0$, where $\partial$ is a cemetery state.
--
--   The **Markov chain generated by $Q$** is given by the jump chain/holding time construction: from $x$ the chain waits an exponential time of rate $Q(x)$ (forever if $Q(x)=0$), then jumps to $y\ne x$ with probability $Q(x,y)/Q(x)$ and to $\partial$ with the remaining probability; after an explosion it is sent to $\partial$. From this construction the file defines
--
--   1. the **transition function** $P_t(x,y)=\mathbb P_x(X_t=y)$, as a sum over jump-chain paths $x=\omega_0,\dots,\omega_n=y$ of the path probability times the probability that the $n$-th jump time is $\le t$ and the $(n+1)$-st is $>t$;
--   2. the **resolvent** $G(x,y)=\int_0^\infty P_t(x,y)\,dt\in[0,\infty]$;
--   3. the hitting probabilities $\mathbb P_x(T_A<\zeta)$ and $\mathbb P_x(T_A<T_B\wedge\zeta)$ and the exit law $\mathbb P_x(X_{T_A}=z,\,T_A<\zeta)$, where $T_A=\inf\{t\ge0:X_t\in A\}$ and $\zeta$ is the lifetime;
--   4. the resolvent $G^A$ of the chain **killed at $T_A$** (state space $E^A=E\setminus A$, the same $Q$ restricted to $E^A$), extended by $0$ off $E^A\times E^A$;
--   5. the **dual** Q-matrix $\widehat Q(y,x)=\pi(x)Q(x,y)/\pi(y)$ with respect to a measure $\pi$, excessive and stationary measures, transience ($G(x,x)<\infty$) and recurrence ($G(x,x)=\infty$) of all states;
--   6. the skip-free downward condition (2.1): $Q(x,x-1)>0$ if $x>\mathfrak l$ and $Q(x,y)=0$ if $y\le x-2$;
--   7. the fundamental functions of Theorem 3.1: $H(x)=\lim_{y\downarrow\mathfrak l}G(x,y)/G(\mathfrak o,y)$, $\widehat H(y)=\lim_{x\uparrow\mathfrak h}\widehat G(y,x)/\widehat G(\mathfrak o,x)$, $\mathbf H^{[b}(x)=\lim_{y\downarrow\mathfrak l}G^{[b}(x,y)/G(\mathfrak o,y)$, and the resolvent densities $\mathfrak g(x,y)=G(x,y)/\pi(y)$, $\mathfrak g^A(x,y)=G^A(x,y)/\pi(y)$.
--
--   These are the objects of Sections 2 and 3 of the paper; every probabilistic quantity of the mission is computed from this single construction.
--
--   **Formalization Note** States are integers and $E$ is an order-connected subset of $\mathbb Z$ with at least two points; leaving $E$ (killing, a jump out of $E$, explosion) represents $\partial$. Probabilities and the resolvent take values in $[0,\infty]$. Holding times are realised as $e_k/Q(\omega_k)$ with i.i.d. standard exponential clocks $e_k$. Where $\mathfrak l=-\infty$ (resp. $\mathfrak h=\infty$) the fundamental functions are limits along $y\to-\infty$ (resp. $x\to\infty$), defined with `limUnder`; otherwise they are the values at the end point. The theorems assert that the limits exist.
-- source:
--   Loeffen, Patie, Wang, Fluctuation Theory of Continuous-Time, Skip-Free Downward Markov Chains with Applications to Branching Processes with Immigration, arXiv:2208.14425v1, pp. 2–5, Section 2, (2.1)–(2.3), and the definitions of H, Ĥ, H^[b in Theorem 3.1

import Mathlib
open scoped ENNReal Topology
open Filter MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Classical

namespace SkipFreeFluct.MBI

/-!
# Continuous-time Markov chains generated by a (possibly non-conservative) Q-matrix

Loeffen, Patie, Wang, arXiv:2208.14425v1, Section 2, pp. 2–4.

States are integers. The state space is a set `E : Set ℤ` which is an integer interval with at
least two points, i.e. `E = [𝔩, 𝔥] ∩ ℤ` with `𝔩 < 𝔥` in `ℤ ∪ {±∞}`. The cemetery state `∂` is not
an integer: mass that is killed (rate `Q(x, ∂)`), that jumps out of `E`, or that explodes simply
leaves `E`.

The chain is the paper's "jump chain/holding time" construction (items (i)–(iv), p. 2):
from state `x` the chain waits an exponential time of rate `Q(x) = -Q(x,x)` (infinite if
`Q(x) = 0`), then jumps to `y ≠ x` with probability `Q(x,y)/Q(x)` and to `∂` with the remaining
probability `Q(x,∂)/Q(x)`; after an explosion it is in `∂`. All probabilistic quantities
(transition function, resolvent, hitting and exit probabilities, killed and dual chains) are
computed from this one construction: sums over finite jump-chain paths, with the holding times
realised as `Exp(1)` clocks divided by the rates.
-/

/-- `E` is an integer interval `[𝔩, 𝔥] ∩ ℤ` with `𝔩 < 𝔥` (`𝔩 = -∞` iff `E` is not bounded below,
`𝔥 = +∞` iff `E` is not bounded above). -/
def IsStateSpace (E : Set ℤ) : Prop :=
  E.OrdConnected ∧ ∃ x ∈ E, ∃ y ∈ E, x < y

/-- The total jump rate `Q(x) := -Q(x, x)`. -/
def rate (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (x : ℤ) : ℝ := -Q x x

/-- The off-diagonal row sum `∑_{y ∈ E, y ≠ x} Q(x, y)`. -/
noncomputable def offDiagSum (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (x : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  ∑' y : E, if (y : ℤ) ≠ x then Q x y else 0

/-- `Q` is a Q-matrix on `E` (p. 2): `0 ≤ Q(x, y) < ∞` for `x ≠ y` and
`∑_{y ≠ x} Q(x, y) ≤ Q(x) < ∞`. Conservativity is **not** assumed. -/
def IsQMatrix (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ x ∈ E, ∀ y ∈ E, x ≠ y → 0 ≤ Q x y) ∧
  ∀ x ∈ E, Summable (fun y : E => if (y : ℤ) ≠ x then Q x y else 0) ∧
    offDiagSum E Q x ≤ rate Q x

/-- The killing rate `Q(x, ∂) := Q(x) - ∑_{y ≠ x} Q(x, y) ≥ 0`. -/
noncomputable def killRate (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (x : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  rate Q x - offDiagSum E Q x

/-- Assumption (2.1), p. 3: `Q(x, x - 1) > 0` if `x > 𝔩` and `Q(x, y) = 0` if `y ≤ x - 2`
(for an integer interval, `x > 𝔩` with `x ∈ E` is `x - 1 ∈ E`). -/
def SkipFreeDown (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ E, (x - 1 ∈ E → 0 < Q x (x - 1)) ∧ ∀ y ∈ E, y ≤ x - 2 → Q x y = 0

/-- One-step transition probability of the jump chain inside `E` (item (iii), p. 2):
`Q(x, y)/Q(x)` for `x, y ∈ E`, `y ≠ x`, `Q(x) > 0`; the missing mass goes to the cemetery. -/
noncomputable def jumpProb (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (x y : ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  if x ∈ E ∧ y ∈ E ∧ y ≠ x ∧ 0 < rate Q x then ENNReal.ofReal (Q x y / rate Q x) else 0

/-- Probability that the jump chain started at `ω 0` follows the path `ω 0, ω 1, …, ω n`
inside `E`. -/
noncomputable def pathWeight (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) {n : ℕ} (ω : Fin (n + 1) → ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∏ k : Fin n, jumpProb E Q (ω k.castSucc) (ω k.succ)

/-- The `k`-th holding time along the path `ω`, realised from a standard exponential clock
`e k ~ Exp(1)`: `e k / Q(ω k)`, which is `Exp(Q(ω k))`-distributed if `Q(ω k) > 0` and `∞` if
`Q(ω k) = 0` (item (ii), p. 2). -/
noncomputable def holdTime (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) {n : ℕ} (ω : Fin (n + 1) → ℤ) (e : Fin (n + 1) → ℝ)
    (k : Fin (n + 1)) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ENNReal.ofReal (e k) / ENNReal.ofReal (rate Q (ω k))

/-- The `n`-th jump time `J_n` along the path `ω`: the sum of the first `n` holding times. -/
noncomputable def jumpTime (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) {n : ℕ} (ω : Fin (n + 1) → ℤ) (e : Fin (n + 1) → ℝ) :
    ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑ k : Fin n, holdTime Q ω e k.castSucc

/-- Law of `n + 1` i.i.d. standard exponential clocks. -/
noncomputable def clockLaw (n : ℕ) : Measure (Fin (n + 1) → ℝ) :=
  Measure.pi (fun _ => expMeasure 1)

/-- The transition function `P_t(x, y) = ℙ_x(X_t = y)`, `x, y ∈ E`, `t ≥ 0` (p. 3), of the
Markov chain generated by `Q` with state space `E`: the chain is at `y` at time `t` after exactly
`n` jumps along the jump-chain path `ω` iff `J_n ≤ t < J_n + H_{n+1}`. Summing over `n` and `ω`
gives `ℙ_x(X_t = y)`; after an explosion no finite `n` contributes (item (iv)). It is `0` when
`x ∉ E` or `y ∉ E`. -/
noncomputable def transition (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (t : ℝ) (x y : ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  if x ∈ E ∧ y ∈ E then
    ∑' n : ℕ, ∑' ω : Fin (n + 1) → ℤ,
      if ω 0 = x ∧ ω (Fin.last n) = y then
        pathWeight E Q ω *
          clockLaw n {e | jumpTime Q ω e ≤ ENNReal.ofReal t ∧
            ENNReal.ofReal t < jumpTime Q ω e + holdTime Q ω e (Fin.last n)}
      else 0
  else 0

/-- The resolvent `G(x, y) = ∫_0^∞ P_t(x, y) dt ∈ [0, ∞]` (p. 3). -/
noncomputable def resolvent (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (x y : ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∫⁻ t in Set.Ici (0 : ℝ), transition E Q t x y

/-- `ℙ_x(T_A < T_B ∧ ζ)`: the chain started at `x ∈ E` enters `A` before it enters `B` and before
its lifetime `ζ`. The time-ordering of the visits is that of the jump chain, so this is the
probability that the jump chain started at `x` reaches `A \ B` at its first visit to `A ∪ B`
(time `0` counts: `x ∈ A \ B` gives `1`). -/
noncomputable def hitBeforeProb (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (A B : Set ℤ) (x : ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  if x ∈ E then
    ∑' n : ℕ, ∑' ω : Fin (n + 1) → ℤ,
      if ω 0 = x ∧ ω (Fin.last n) ∈ A \ B ∧ ∀ k : Fin n, ω k.castSucc ∉ A ∪ B then
        pathWeight E Q ω
      else 0
  else 0

/-- `ℙ_x(T_A < ζ)`, the probability that the chain started at `x` ever visits `A`. -/
noncomputable def hitProb (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (A : Set ℤ) (x : ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  hitBeforeProb E Q A ∅ x

/-- The exit distribution `ℙ_x(X_{T_A} = z, T_A < ζ)`. -/
noncomputable def exitDist (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (A : Set ℤ) (x z : ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  if x ∈ E then
    ∑' n : ℕ, ∑' ω : Fin (n + 1) → ℤ,
      if ω 0 = x ∧ ω (Fin.last n) = z ∧ z ∈ A ∧ ∀ k : Fin n, ω k.castSucc ∉ A then
        pathWeight E Q ω
      else 0
  else 0

/-- The resolvent `G^A` of the chain killed at `T_A` (p. 4): the chain with state space
`E^A = E \ A` generated by `Q^A(x, y) = Q(x, y)`, `x, y ∈ E^A` (jumps into `A` are sent to the
cemetery), extended by `0` outside `E^A × E^A`. -/
noncomputable def killedResolvent (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (A : Set ℤ) (x y : ℤ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  if x ∈ E \ A ∧ y ∈ E \ A then resolvent (E \ A) Q x y else 0

/-- The Q-matrix of the dual chain with respect to `π` (p. 3):
`Q̂(y, x) = π(x) Q(x, y) / π(y)`. -/
noncomputable def dualQ (π : ℤ → ℝ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (y x : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  π x * Q x y / π y

/-- `π` is an excessive measure on `E` (p. 3): `π ≥ 0` and
`∑_{x ∈ E} π(x) P_t(x, y) ≤ π(y)` for all `y ∈ E`, `t ≥ 0`. -/
def IsExcessiveMeasure (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (π : ℤ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ x ∈ E, 0 ≤ π x) ∧
  ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → ∀ y ∈ E,
    ∑' x : E, ENNReal.ofReal (π x) * transition E Q t x y ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (π y)

/-- `π` is a stationary measure on `E` (p. 3): `π ≥ 0` and
`∑_{x ∈ E} π(x) P_t(x, y) = π(y)` for all `y ∈ E`, `t ≥ 0`. -/
def IsStationaryMeasure (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (π : ℤ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ x ∈ E, 0 ≤ π x) ∧
  ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → ∀ y ∈ E,
    ∑' x : E, ENNReal.ofReal (π x) * transition E Q t x y = ENNReal.ofReal (π y)

/-- All states of `E` are transient: `G(x, x) = ∫_0^∞ P_t(x, x) dt < ∞` for every `x ∈ E`
(Norris, *Markov Chains*, Theorem 3.4.2, used by the paper on p. 3). -/
def AllTransient (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ E, resolvent E Q x x < ⊤

/-- All states of `E` are recurrent: `G(x, x) = ∞` for every `x ∈ E`. -/
def AllRecurrent (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ E, resolvent E Q x x = ⊤

/-- The fundamental excessive function of Theorem 3.1(1), p. 5, with reference point `o`:
`H(x) = lim_{y ↓ 𝔩} G(x, y)/G(o, y)`, i.e. `G(x, 𝔩)/G(o, 𝔩)` if `𝔩 > -∞` and the limit along
`y → -∞` if `𝔩 = -∞` (`limUnder` is junk when no limit exists; the theorems assert it exists). -/
noncomputable def fundH (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (o x : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  if BddBelow E then
    (resolvent E Q x (sInf E)).toReal / (resolvent E Q o (sInf E)).toReal
  else
    limUnder atBot (fun y : ℤ => (resolvent E Q x y).toReal / (resolvent E Q o y).toReal)

/-- The dual fundamental function of Theorem 3.1(3), p. 5:
`Ĥ(y) = lim_{x ↑ 𝔥} Ĝ(y, x)/Ĝ(o, x)`, with `Ĝ` the resolvent of the dual chain (generated by
`dualQ π Q` on `E`): `Ĝ(y, 𝔥)/Ĝ(o, 𝔥)` if `𝔥 < ∞`, the limit along `x → ∞` if `𝔥 = ∞`. -/
noncomputable def fundHhat (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (π : ℤ → ℝ) (o y : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  if BddAbove E then
    (resolvent E (dualQ π Q) y (sSup E)).toReal / (resolvent E (dualQ π Q) o (sSup E)).toReal
  else
    limUnder atTop (fun x : ℤ =>
      (resolvent E (dualQ π Q) y x).toReal / (resolvent E (dualQ π Q) o x).toReal)

/-- The killed fundamental function of Theorem 3.1(3), p. 5:
`H^{[b}(x) = lim_{y ↓ 𝔩} G^{[b}(x, y)/G(o, y)`, where `G^{[b}` is the resolvent of the chain
killed on entering `[b, ∞)`; same case split as `fundH`. -/
noncomputable def fundHb (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (o b x : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  if BddBelow E then
    (killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ici b) x (sInf E)).toReal / (resolvent E Q o (sInf E)).toReal
  else
    limUnder atBot (fun y : ℤ =>
      (killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ici b) x y).toReal / (resolvent E Q o y).toReal)

/-- The resolvent density `𝔤(x, y) = G(x, y)/π(y)` (p. 3). -/
noncomputable def rdens (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (π : ℤ → ℝ) (x y : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  (resolvent E Q x y).toReal / π y

/-- The density `𝔤^A(x, y) = G^A(x, y)/π(y)` of the killed resolvent (p. 4). -/
noncomputable def killedRdens (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (π : ℤ → ℝ) (A : Set ℤ) (x y : ℤ) : ℝ :=
  (killedResolvent E Q A x y).toReal / π y

end SkipFreeFluct.MBI


